@attribute [Route(WebUiModule.OperatorStatusPath)]
@attribute [Authorize(Policy = OperatorAccess.Policy)]
@using Ecnanib.Accounts

@*
    The operator status screen (FR-UI-2). It is for operators alone: a visitor is sent to sign
    in, and a user who is not an operator is refused (NFR-SEC-3). It has a route and a place in
    the bar of an operator, and only says what it is to show (FR-OPS-2). It has no form, asks
    the database nothing, and shows nothing of any user (FR-OPS-5): a screen that only shows is
    no action of an operator, so nothing of it is recorded in the audit trail. The first form
    here is such an action. What an operator does is on a page of its own, which this screen
    leads to with a link: the global halt (FR-OPS-3). See "Operators" in docs/ownership.md.
*@

<PageTitle>@Screens.OperatorStatus.Name</PageTitle>

<h1>@Screens.OperatorStatus.Name</h1>

<p>@OperatorPages.ForOperators</p>

<p>@OperatorPages.NotBuiltYet</p>

<p>@OperatorPages.OnlyShows</p>

<p><a href="@WebUiModule.GlobalHaltPath">@OperatorPages.HaltTitle</a></p>
